$ORIGIN kyriakon.net.
$TTL 3600

; kyriakon.net - hidden-primary zone file.
; On-box path: /var/nsd/etc/kyriakon.net.zone.
; All IPs below are RFC 5737 (203.0.113.0/24) and RFC 3849 (2001:db8::/32)
; documentation placeholders - substitute the box's real Hetzner IPv4/IPv6
; before deploy.

@	IN	SOA	ns0.kyriakon.net. hostmaster.kyriakon.net. (
		2026091801	; serial - YYYYMMDDNN, bump on EVERY edit (see note below)
		3600		; refresh - HE re-checks at least this often
		900		; retry
		1209600		; expire - 14 days: HE keeps serving if the primary dies
		3600		; negative-cache TTL
		)

; SERIAL-BUMP DISCIPLINE: the SOA serial is the single source of "has this zone
; changed" for both NOTIFY-triggered and refresh-timer transfers. If you edit
; this file and forget to bump the serial, HE's secondaries keep serving the
; stale zone. Bump it on every edit.

; Public delegation: HE's anycast secondaries ONLY. The hidden primary
; (ns0 / this box) is deliberately ABSENT from NS - hidden, not public.
@	IN	NS	ns1.he.net.
@	IN	NS	ns2.he.net.
@	IN	NS	ns3.he.net.
@	IN	NS	ns4.he.net.
@	IN	NS	ns5.he.net.

; SOA MNAME resolves to the hidden primary so tooling (`dig SOA`) can reach it,
; but it is not listed in NS.
ns0	IN	A	203.0.113.10
ns0	IN	AAAA	2001:db8::10

; Apex - the box's real IPs. Mail, SSH/git, Gemini, and the landing site all
; resolve here.
@	IN	A	203.0.113.10
@	IN	AAAA	2001:db8::10

; MX - mail delivered to the box. Single MX, no secondary in MVP.
@	IN	MX	10 mail.kyriakon.net.
mail	IN	A	203.0.113.10
mail	IN	AAAA	2001:db8::10

; SPF - the box is the only sender. "mx" authorizes the MX host; "-all"
; hard-fails everything else.
@	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 mx -all"

; SPF for the mail host itself. The host sends mail as its own hostname: cron
; output, the daily security(8) mail, and smtpd's bounces from MAILER-DAEMON
; all carry mail.kyriakon.net as both the envelope and the From domain, so SPF
; is evaluated against this name rather than the apex. With no record here the
; check returns "none", that message gets no SPF pass, and DMARC then rests on
; DKIM alone. Google's aggregate report for 2026-09-15 showed exactly that:
; spf=fail on every row from this box, accepted on the DKIM signature.
;
; The mechanism is "a", not "mx". This name has no MX record of its own, so an
; mx lookup would match nothing and authorize nobody.
mail	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 a -all"

; DKIM - public half only, at selector "mail". The private key lives on the box
; at /etc/mail/dkim/private.rsa.key (the path smtpd.conf's dkimsign filter
; reads, owned by _dkimsign, mode 0600) and is NEVER in this repo.
; deploy-mail.sh prints this base64 value when the on-box key does not match
; what is published here, which is how it was generated.
;
; The value is 410 bytes, and a TXT character-string caps at 255, so the record
; is written as two adjacent quoted strings. Resolvers concatenate them into the
; single string DKIM expects. Publishing it as one quoted string makes the zone
; unparseable, and nsd then serves nothing at all for the domain rather than
; complaining.
mail._domainkey	IN	TXT	( "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEAzD06rNwCr6k6jHwH5TTqB1dgnIS2TehRQ88ygp++duHGV7S9TGaxblMeiiCcMe/BOE5KJy6qHUjOM/POB/wLY7i0+nYhlMV5dUW67oGVX68dOFDj63V6uR/SqotPFLVU+uVFzx79LAGm3HogwwmYiAa5RlwsRaYPjS/pyqEEQaVWVa1qMo85Fvwb0JYkjERAx"
				"TTJ5IwH9Fe1zqt5qL2jazc6UB2jzb5weWgVm167uvxNkn37FqDl/GHDJATi+hJoq2iLtiSHXru1a4iARZmJCih+2Ak9fA3NF/fI1EfqqS3xU7P4zzdUnOvR+GQ2Qz4L+jRUvUX9yHu/8FIZ09ssywIDAQAB" )

; DMARC now enforces quarantine on authentication failures. The record started as
; p=none with aggregate reporting so the first reports could be measured, and the
; Google report for 2026-09-18 showed spf=pass and dkim=pass on every row, which
; was the condition recorded in the research note for tightening the policy.
; Quarantine comes before reject because the first enforcement step should not be
; able to bounce a legitimate sender outright.
_dmarc	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:dmarc@kyriakon.net"

; Wildcard - one record serves every per-user subdomain (username.kyriakon.net).
; A record, NOT a cert: acme-client is HTTP-01 only, so per-user certs are
; issued individually per signup.
*	IN	A	203.0.113.10
*	IN	AAAA	2001:db8::10
